विपरी वि-परी (-परि-इ), cl. 2. P. -पर्य्-एति,
-एतुम्, to go or turn round in an opposite direction;
to turn round the wrong way; to go round, return.

विपादिका वि-पादिका, f. (fr. पाद with वि),
a disease of the foot, a sore or tumour on the foot;
a riddle, enigma.

विप्रकृ वि-प्र-कृ, cl. 8. P. A. -करोति, -कु-
रुते, -कर्तुम्, to treat with disrespect, hurt, injure;
to offend, disturb, oppress.

विप्रस्था वि-प्र-स्था, cl. 1. A. (sometimes
P.) -तिष्ठते (-ति), -स्थातुम्, to go away, depart;
to extend, be extended.

विप्लुष् वि-प्लुष्, ट्, f. (also written वि-प्रुष्;
see rts. प्लुष्, 1. प्रुष्), a drop of any fluid; a
spot, dot.
